### Page 1 of 1

```text
RESOLUTION NO. ________

ENTITLED: “A RESOLUTION DIRECTING CHEYENNE FIRE AND RESCUE TO
EVALUATE
ALL
FACILITIES
AND
OPERATIONS
OF
THE
CHEYENNE FIRE AND RESCUE DEPARTMENT.”

WHEREAS, the City of Cheyenne is facing an unprecedented budget crisis and the
current costs of services are unsustainable; and

WHEREAS, the City of Cheyenne Fire and Rescue Department has the second largest
General Fund budget in the City of Cheyenne encompassing twenty (20) percent of all General
Fund expenditures; and

WHEREAS, the City of Cheyenne is in great need of new facilities for Cheyenne Fire
and Rescue, including several new fire stations; and

WHEREAS, the Governing Body has seen other communities maintain budget
predictability with alternative responses to public safety including privatization of some fire
departments; and

WHEREAS, the Governing Body will benefit from a full cost-benefit analysis of
Cheyenne Fire and Rescue to assist with decision making moving forward; and

WHEREAS, the Governing Body directs the Chief of the Cheyenne Fire and Rescue
Department to investigate and evaluate every aspect of the Department including, but not limited
to, operations, staffing, facilities, training, prevention, call-response times, equipment and
general public safety and prepare a report outlining these costs; and

WHEREAS, the Governing Body requests that this report be completed and presented no
later than July 31, 2021 to prepare for future budget cycles.

NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED BY THE GOVERNING BODY OF THE
CITY OF CHEYENNE, WYOMING, that the Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne
requires the Cheyenne Fire and Rescue Department to present a full review of all operations and
facilities of the Cheyenne Fire and Rescue Department by July 31, 2021.

PRESENTED, READ, AND ADOPTED this ______ day of __________________,
2021.

CITY OF CHEYENNE

BY:

_________________________________________

Patrick Collins, Mayor
(SEAL)

ATTEST:

__________________________________
Kristina F. Jones, City Clerk

By Alessandra at 9:39 am, Mar 19, 2021
```
